## Various simple aggregation measures for use in the scenario model engine and reporting outputs.

#######################################################
## This specific measure is used to calculate the total value and divide by 1000 to convert to $bn for reporting purposes.
## It is used in the scenario model engine to derive post-tax metrics and other financial calculations.

Value $bn:=DIVIDE(SUM([Value]),1000)

#######################################################
## This specific measure is used to calculate the inverted value in $bn for reporting purposes.
## Capex, Opex, DD&A, and other cost metrics are typically reported as negative values in the scenario model engine, and this measure provides a way to present them as positive values in the reporting outputs.

Inv Value $bn:=[Value $bn]*-1

#######################################################
## This specific measure is used to calculate the total value formatted for reporting purposes.
## It was used as Pivot tables kept defaulting to a format not suitable for the scenario model engine outputs, and this measure provides a consistent way to present the values in the reporting outputs.

Value Formatted:=SUM([Value])

#######################################################
## This specific measure is used to calculate the post-tax NPV in $bn for reporting purposes.
## It is used in the scenario model engine to derive post-tax metrics and other financial calculations, and it filters the ScenarioResults table to include only the rows where the Metric is "Discounted Post-Tax Cash Flow @ 8%".

Post-Tax NPV $bn:=CALCULATE(
    SUM(ScenarioResults[Value]),
    ScenarioResults[Metric] = "Discounted Post-Tax Cash Flow @ 8%"
) / 1000